## Why This Is Asked
To assess practical knowledge of session security with minimal risk and knowledge of CSRF.

## Key Concepts
- HttpOnly and SameSite cookies
- CSRF protection strategies (double-submit, token rotation)
- Token rotation for refresh tokens
- Minimal server middleware for validation
- Secure login/logout flows

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal Express middleware for cookie-based auth
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
function authMiddleware(req, res, next){
  const token = req.cookies?.access_token;
  if(!token) return res.status(401).send('Unauthorized');
  try {
    req.user = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET);
    // rotation logic if near expiry would be here
    next();
  } catch {
    res.status(401).send('Unauthorized');
  }
}
```

